This software ("INNLI") is licensed, not sold. By installing or using INNLI
you accept these terms.

1. Trial version
   You may install and use INNLI free of charge without a licence key to try
   it. Without a valid licence key an installation is not listed in the INNLI
   guide.

2. Licence after payment
   After payment you receive a licence key. It gives you a non-exclusive,
   non-transferable and perpetual right to use INNLI:
   a. on one installation;
   b. for the number of properties stated in the licence key;
   c. for all versions released during the update period stated in the
      licence key. After the update period you may keep using the last
      version from that period without limit.

3. What is not allowed
   Without the Supplier's written permission you may not:
   a. sell, rent out, give away or otherwise make INNLI, or a modified
      version of it, available to third parties;
   b. offer INNLI as a service to others (for example as hosting or SaaS);
   c. circumvent the licence check, or share a licence key or use it on more
      installations than allowed;
   d. build your own guide or a similar service based on INNLI.
   You may modify INNLI for your own use within your licence. Web designers
   who install INNLI for clients need a separate licence per client.

4. Third-party components
   INNLI contains open-source components of third parties. Their own licences
   apply; they are included in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt and in the
   node_modules folder. The WordPress plugin (wordpress-plugin folder) is
   licensed under GPL-2.0-or-later, as is usual for WordPress plugins.

5. Your data
   INNLI runs on your own device or server. Your data and your guests' data
   stay there. You are the controller of that data within the meaning of
   the GDPR. The Supplier receives no guest data. The INNLI guide only
   receives data you make public: name, place, short description and the
   address of your installation. You are responsible for your own backups.

6. Warranty and liability
   INNLI is provided as is. The Supplier makes reasonable efforts to fix
   errors during the update period, but does not guarantee that INNLI works
   without errors or interruptions. INNLI does not make bookings in external
   systems and does not guarantee findability or a position in search
   engines or AI assistants. The Supplier's liability is limited to the
   amount you paid for the licence. The Supplier is not liable for indirect
   damage, such as lost revenue, missed or double bookings or loss of data,
   except in case of intent or gross negligence.

7. Business use
   The licence is intended for entrepreneurs who use INNLI for their
   business.

8. Termination
   If you act in breach of these terms, your licence lapses and the licence
   key may be refused in the INNLI guide. Amounts paid are not refunded.

9. Applicable law
   These terms are governed by Dutch law. Disputes are submitted to the
   competent court in the district of the Supplier.
